   finetune), NOT derived from the pinned qwen3_5_9b set. The framing leans into
   IMMERSIVE in-character SCENE voice so the sim is more interesting: the meeting
   is a tense moment the character is living through. Because RP finetunes drift
   from output format, the JSON discipline is stated extra firmly — in-character
   voice lives ONLY inside the free_text field; everything else is strict JSON.

   Output: ONE meetings.schemas.MeetingTurn (turn_kind = "opening"). The meeting
   manager overrides the identity fields after parsing. The output JSON schema is
   the ONE hard invariant shared across every prompt set (owner decision
   2026-06-30) so model_validate_json + the recording seam are set-independent.

   Inputs (the loader kwargs this template may reference; nothing else, so no
   hidden engine state reaches the LLM — DESIGN.md §1.3 observation firewall):
     agent_id, current_tick, meeting_trigger, rendered_memory, public_transcript,
